## Implementation Steps

### 1. Set up Devise

First, set up Devise for basic authentication:

```bash
rails generate devise:install
rails generate devise User
rails db:migrate
```

### 2. Configure WebAuthn

Add this to your `config/initializers/webauthn.rb`:

```ruby
Webauthn.configure do |config|
  config.issuer = "My App" # Your application name
  config.origin = "http://localhost:3000" # Change this to your production URL
  config.rp_id = "localhost" # This should match the origin without protocol
  config.rp_name = "My App"
  config.rp_icon = "https://your-domain.com/logo.png" # Optional
  config.attestation_conveyance_preference = "none" # For production, consider "none" or "indirect"
  config.accept = ["public-key"] # Only allow public-key credentials
  config.challenge_method = :secure_random
  config.timeout = 30000 # 30 seconds
  config.authenticator_selection = {
    require_resident_key: true,
    user_verification: "preferred"
  }
end
```

### 3. Add WebAuthn to User Model

```ruby
# app/models/user.rb
class User < ApplicationRecord
  devise :database_authenticatable, :registerable,
         :recoverable, :rememberable, :validatable

  # WebAuthn credentials
  has_many :webauthn_credentials, dependent: :destroy
  accepts_nested_attributes_for :webauthn_credentials

  # For WebAuthn
  def credential_ids
    webauthn_credentials.map(&:credential_id)
  end

  def credentials_for_sign_in
    webauthn_credentials.where.not(credential_id: nil)
  end
end
```

### 4. Create WebAuthn Credential Model

```bash
rails generate model WebauthnCredential user:references credential_id:string public_key:string created_at:datetime updated_at:datetime
rails db:migrate
```

Then update the model:

```ruby
# app/models/webauthn_credential.rb
class WebauthnCredential < ApplicationRecord
  belongs_to :user

  def credential_id
    Base64.strict_encode64(self[:credential_id])
  end

  def credential_id=(value)
    self[:credential_id] = Base64.strict_decode64(value)
  end

  def public_key
    Base64.strict_encode64(self[:public_key])
  end

  def public_key=(value)
    self[:public_key] = Base64.strict_decode64(value)
